Modifications in this fork
--------------------------

The fork tracks upstream `main` and adds:

  * Bedrock/Geyser crossplay on top of Java servers (backend/bedrock/):
      - one-click install of GeyserMC and Floodgate into a Java server's
        plugins directory,
      - automatic playit.gg provisioning of two UDP tunnels per server —
        NetherNet and RakNet — through the playit.gg API, so Bedrock clients
        can join either way without port-forwarding,
      - patching of Geyser's config.yml (both transports, per-transport ports,
        NetherNet signaling token, Floodgate auth),
      - panel UI to enable/disable crossplay and show both resulting addresses
        (frontend/src/views/server/*, frontend/src/stores/bedrock.js,
        frontend/src/api/bedrock.js).
  * Self-updater and release tooling pointed at this fork
    (backend/repo.py, backend/system/update_service.py, tools/cli.py,
    tools/install.sh, .github/workflows/release.yml, docker-compose.yml).
  * Removal of the upstream-only Cloudflare website deploy workflow.
  * Docs for the crossplay feature and the fork's release process.

All other code is upstream Fabricator, unmodified except where required to
integrate the changes above. The complete corresponding source for every
release of this fork is the tagged tree in this repository:

    https://github.com/TheDevfromDevshome/Fabricator

Because Fabricator is network server software, AGPL-3.0 section 13 applies:
users interacting with a deployed instance are entitled to the source of the
version being run. That is this repository at the deployed release tag.

Upstream credits and the original project's documentation, website
(https://fabricator.site) and community remain the canonical references for
